  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015): the contrast CT is ordered and the RBC-RAD-07 prep is done.\n- **CT order:** CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast, pancreatic protocol for the pancreatic cyst check (sr-t0001). It's set for Mon 10/26 at 9:00 and linked to that appointment (§5).\n- **Reaction grade:** the 2019 iohexol (CT dye) reaction counts as moderate. The radiology report from that day describes hives and eyelid swelling with normal breathing and blood pressure, and calls it moderate. The 'anaphylaxis' label on his allergy list was added in 2021 from his own account, with no records reviewed. Under §1 that label doesn't change the grade, so this is not a severe reaction (§3). I left the allergy list unchanged and explained this in the CT order and the chart note. His shellfish and povidone-iodine (Betadine) allergies don't count as risk factors.\n- **Premedication (§2):** prednisone 50 mg by mouth at 8:00 PM Sun 10/25, 2:00 AM Mon and 8:00 AM Mon (mr-t0002). Diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth at 8:00 AM Mon (mr-t0003). He must not drive after it and needs a driver.\n- **Kidney check before the scan (§4):** he is 64 and has diabetes. His last normal creatinine (9/24) is 32 days before the scan, just outside the 30-day window. The ER values from 10/16–17 were drawn during a kidney injury from dehydration (creatinine 1.94, then 1.46), so they don't count. I ordered a new creatinine to be drawn before the scan, between now and 8:30 AM Monday (sr-t0004). The scan stays as booked, and the radiologist reviews the result that morning.\n- **Metformin (§6):** because of the kidney injury, metformin is on hold. His last dose is Sunday evening, none from Monday morning, and it stays off for at least 48 hours after the scan. It restarts only once his kidney function is rechecked and normal. A follow-up creatinine is ordered for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006), which also covers the ER's request for a one-week recheck. You have a task due 10/30 to review that result and decide when he restarts (task-t0007).\n- **Patient instructions:** sent to his portal (comm-t0008). They cover the blood draw, the medicine times, the driver, stopping metformin, arriving at 8:45 and warning signs.\n- **Chart note:** documents all of the above and cites RBC-RAD-07 (doc-t0009).",
